  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, the only ways in which an user can rebind non-VR controller bindings are to either force SteamInput on and create a custom profile, or to use an external rebinding application such as DS4Windows.\n\nBoth approaches are undesirable, as they cause a number of issues.\n\n1. The in-game prompts will not show the correct rebinded button, as it is not aware that anything has changed.\n\n2. If SteamInput is forced on, the incorrect controller button prompt type will appear since SteamInput emulates an XInput device.\n\n3. SteamInput is unavailable on non-Steam versions of VRChat (such as the VIVEPORT distribution), so the use of external rebinding tools such as DS4Windows is required.\n\nTo resolve this, a native way to rebind non-VR controls from within VRChat itself should be added.",
